{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>לשמרך</b> — The reproofs are לשמרך, to guard you from an evil woman, for she is worse than all transgressions, for she draws evil in her wake; she apportion charm to a woman that her tongue may speak smoothly, and a married woman [זרה] is the ornament of the tongue."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:21:12.641791615Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}